      "level": 2,
      "content": "2.1 Location & Extent"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Chhattisgarh's geography is structured into four primary physiographic divisions: Northern Hills, Chhattisgarh Plain (Maidan), Dandakaranya, and Jashpur Plateau.",
        "The Southern Hilly Region of the state is known as Dandakaranya.",
        "The Eastern Hills section of Chhattisgarh is defined by the Jashpur Plateau.",
        "Core topics in Chhattisgarh geography cover Location & Extent, Rivers, Mountains & Peaks, Climate, and Districts."
      ],
      "id": "ldpqlx0"
